---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Meeting Pulse docs | Install, pair, and troubleshoot"
  description="Practical Meeting Pulse docs for macOS installation, Accessibility permission, pairing a viewer, recovery, and unavailable states."
  canonicalPath="/docs/"
>
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav />
    <article class="docs-content">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Docs" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
      <h1>Use the owner app. Share the smallest useful signal.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl)">
        These pages cover the public setup path for Meeting Pulse. They explain
        what the app needs, what the viewer shows, and what to do when the
        signal is unavailable.
      </p>

      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/install-macos/">Install Meeting Pulse on macOS</a></li>
        <li><a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/accessibility-permission/">Understand Accessibility permission</a></li>
        <li><a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/pairing/">Pair a private viewer</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When something looks wrong</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Read the state and troubleshoot it</a></li>
        <li><a class="link-arrow" href="/docs/recovery/">Recover the owner setup</a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Meeting Pulse is not a realtime system.</strong>
        <p>
          A viewer can be stale or disconnected. The product uses explicit
          unavailable states instead of silently assuming someone is free.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
